{"Title":"An Act establishing a tax credit for families caring for relatives with aphasia","BillNumber":"S1907","DocketNumber":"SD301","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"PMO","Name":"Patrick M. O'Connor","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PMO","ResponseDate":"2023-01-12T13:30:04.44"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"PMO","Name":"Patrick M. O'Connor","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PMO","ResponseDate":"2023-01-12T13:30:04.44"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S1907/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. O'Connor, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 1907) of Patrick M. O'Connor for legislation to establish a tax credit for families caring for relatives with aphasia.  Revenue.","DocumentText":"\tSection 6 of chapter 62 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2008 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting after paragraph (a) the following new paragraph:—\r\n\t(b) A credit of $1,000 shall be allowed against the taxes due if the taxpayer has provided more than one-half of the support for a relative diagnosed with aphasia, provided that the relative resided with the taxpayer for more than 6 months of the taxable year. If the credit provided in this section reduces the tax to zero, the taxpayer shall be entitled to a refund equal to the amount by which the amount of the credit exceeded the amount of tax due.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J26","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J26"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}